index 5da8004..b92b7de 100644
--- "a/.checks\\ChangedRowsBaseline\\README.md"
+++ b/README.md
@@ -123,3 +123,5 @@ Truck properties: Reset to original values previews a restoration against the va
 Editors > Addons shows current (original) values for Price, Unlock rank and Exploration unlock. Select and edit their cells, or use Reset selected to original / Reset to original values, then Stage changes and Start > Apply pending changes. Revert unstaged edits restores the saved snapshot; Revert staged changes clears it. Blank removes the local attribute and restores inheritance. Apply validates exact source, definition and attribute targets before writing; original files and unrelated properties remain intact. Later upgrade randomization can recalculate exploration flags. Packing and installation remain manual.
 
 Editors > Addons follows Truck properties for Price, Unlock rank and Exploration unlock: editable cells, current (original) formatting, green applied/amber preview highlights, Reset selected to original, Reset to original values across both views and filters, Stage changes, Revert unstaged edits and Revert staged changes. Reset restores all three supported properties, including removing local attributes absent from the original. Price accepts whole numbers 0-100,000,000, rank 0-30, exploration true/false; blank restores inheritance. Each staged property identifies its source file, definition variant and attribute; legacy exploration-only snapshots remain readable. Other metadata and physical component parameters remain visible as source properties; engines and winches retain their specialized editors. Apply writes the workspace only, with original files preserved.
+
+Truck properties, Addons and Frame addons each have a Show changed only toggle button. It includes preview/staged differences from current files and applied values differing from preserved originals. In Frame addons this includes fuel and tracked price/rank/exploration changes. It combines with header filters and stays enabled across reloads and addon-view switches; turning it off retains other filters. The toggle changes visibility only: Stage and global reset actions still include hidden rows.
